<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n75777" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδέτερ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>not either, neither of the two</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.51
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ra.</u>
				1412
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phlb.</u>
				21e
			</span></i>: in pl., when each party is pl., first in <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				638
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Sc.</u>
				171
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.76
			</span></i>, etc.: divisim, 
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕτερος</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				1
			</span></i>. Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδετέρως</span>
			<i>in neither of two ways</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				902c
			</span></i>: also neut. pl. as Adv., 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδετέρως</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Plt.</u>
				258a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Tht.</u>
				184a
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>neutral</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν μὲν αἱρετῶν οὐσῶν,
				τῶν δὲ φευκτῶν, τῶν δ᾽ οὐ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>EN</u>
				1175b26
			</span></i>: so in Medic., of a state which is neither illness nor
			health, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διάθεσις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Herophil.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				6.388
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σῶμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					1.307
				</span></i>
			,<i><span class="en">
				311
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> in Gramm.,
				<i>neuter</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρσενικῶν καὶ θηλυκῶν
				καὶ οὐ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				<u>Amm.</u>
				2.10
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ οὐ</span>. (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γένος</span>) the <i>neuter</i> gender, <i><span class="en">
				A.D.
				<u>Pron.</u>
				6.19
			</span></i>. Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ρως</span>
			<i>in the neuter</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Synt.</u>
				199.20
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				9.458
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				15.701a
			</span></i>; also of Verbs, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδετέρα
			διάθεσις</span> Sch.D.T.<i><span class="en">
				p.246
			</span></i> H.</div>
